From: serg987 <50438876+serg987@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: Allow cache hints on the CAPTURE queue

Cedrus never sets allow_cache_hints on its vb2 queues, so
vb2_set_flags_and_caps() always clears V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT
and never reports V4L2_BUF_CAP_SUPPORTS_MMAP_CACHE_HINTS. On a
non-dma-coherent SoC this forces vb2_dc_alloc() down the coherent
path, i.e. CAPTURE buffers (the decoded frames) are always mapped
write-combined, both for mmap() and for the exported dmabuf.

Measured on a sun55i-a523 (Cedrus at 432 MHz, 4K H.264): CPU readback
of a decoded frame (hwdownload in FFmpeg, as used by any userspace
consumer that needs the picture in regular memory, e.g. object
detection in an NVR) runs at ~190 ms/frame over write-combined memory,
i.e. slower than decoding the same stream in software on the CPU.
Allowing cache hints on the CAPTURE queue lets userspace opt in to
V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT (vb2_dc_alloc_non_coherent(), backed by
dma_alloc_noncontiguous()), after which the CPU reads a normal cached
mapping and only the DQBUF-time invalidate (vb2_dc_finish()) touches
the cache. This drops the same readback below 15 ms/frame.

This is opt-in: userspace that does not request the flag keeps the
existing coherent buffers and existing behaviour is unchanged.
Precedent for CAPTURE queues setting allow_cache_hints on a similarly
non-coherent ARM SoC: mtk_vcodec_dec.c (CEDRUS_CAPABILITY comment
aside, see mtk_vcodec_dec_queue_init()).

Signed-off-by: serg987 <50438876+serg987@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -610,6 +610,7 @@ int cedrus_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq,

 	dst_vq->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE;
 	dst_vq->io_modes = VB2_MMAP | VB2_DMABUF;
+	dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	dst_vq->drv_priv = ctx;
 	dst_vq->buf_struct_size = sizeof(struct cedrus_buffer);
 	dst_vq->ops = &cedrus_qops;
